{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-124215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=8u-6v+2,\\,y=4u-3v-1.\n$$\n\nSuppose that $A$ is the matrix that represents the linear transformation associated with $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=1$\n- The transformation is invertible" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8u-6v+2 \\\\ 4u-3v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8u-6v \\\\ 4u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}|=(-3)\\cdot 8-(-6)\\cdot 4=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)=0,$ the affine transformation is *not* invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c67f98e447853b9489432463be401ef6e7cedb7246a49161b503e29f4c4fc198"} {"question" "q-124215" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124215" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124215" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u-6v-2,\\,y=5v-u+9.\n$$\n\nSuppose that $A$ is the matrix that represents the linear transformation associated with $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=4$\n- The transformation is invertible" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-6v-2 \\\\ 5v-u+9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-6v \\\\ -u+5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|=5\\cdot 2-(-6)\\cdot (-1)=4\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $det(A)\\ne 0,$ the affine transformation is invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c67f98e447853b9489432463be401ef6e7cedb7246a49161b503e29f4c4fc198"} {"question" "q-124213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following affine transformations are invertible?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}5u-2v-5 \\\\ 10u-4v+1\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u-v-4 \\\\ u+5v+7\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2u+4v-2 \\\\ 3u+6v+3\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThe transformation is invertible if the matrix $A$ is invertible. That is, if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not invertible. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-2v-5 \\\\ 10u-4v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-2v \\\\ 10u-4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 10 & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 10 & -4\\end{aligned}|=-4\\cdot 5-(-2)\\cdot 10=0.\n$$\n\nSince the determinant is zero, ${T}_{1}$ is *not* invertible.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is invertible. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v-4 \\\\ u+5v+7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ u+5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|=5\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 1=6\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nSince the determinant is nonzero, ${T}_{2}$ is invertible.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not invertible. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u+4v-2 \\\\ 3u+6v+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u+4v \\\\ 3u+6v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}|=6\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nSince the determinant is zero, ${T}_{3}$ is *not* invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c67f98e447853b9489432463be401ef6e7cedb7246a49161b503e29f4c4fc198"} {"question" "q-124210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${T}_{2}$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=4u+2v-5,\\,y=2u+v+6.\n$$\n\nSuppose that $A$ is the matrix that represents the linear transformation associated with $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=0$\n- The transformation is invertible" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4u+2v-5 \\\\ 2u+v+6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u+2v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 2=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)=0,$ the affine transformation is *not* invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124219" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c67f98e447853b9489432463be401ef6e7cedb7246a49161b503e29f4c4fc198"} {"question" "q-124219" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124219" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124219" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=u-v,\\,y=u+2v+1.\n$$\n\nSuppose that $A$ is the matrix that represents the linear transformation associated with $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=0$\n- The transformation is invertible" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ u+2v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ u+2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1=3\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $det(A)\\ne 0,$ the affine transformation is invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c67f98e447853b9489432463be401ef6e7cedb7246a49161b503e29f4c4fc198"} {"question" "q-124111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & 5 \\\\ b & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot (-2)-5\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-3+(-1)+8=4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c67f98e447853b9489432463be401ef6e7cedb7246a49161b503e29f4c4fc198"} {"question" "q-124244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040441/state.json" "file_sha256" "1ecba6ddb51ebffbbf3aecdfa2dffaedfca50f5520271906b7096c58abde30e6"} {"question" "q-124228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 